\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 # Technical Report: Modular Analytics Pipeline & System Governance
\par 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 **Course:** NUS AI/ML & Data Science Capstone (Part 2)  
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 **Environment:** Python 3.12 (`.venv` Isolated Environment)  
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 **Deliverables:** `main.py`, `feature_engineering.py`, `visualization.py`, `pipeline.log`, `outputs/`
\par 
\par ---
\par 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 ## 1. Executive Summary & Infrastructure Governance
\par 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
This project delivers a production-ready, modular command-line interface (CLI) application for urban traffic analytics. Built to meet strict software engineering standards, the system decouples data transformation logic from invocation interfaces. 
\par 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 To resolve **Interpreter Drift**\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 a common issue on Windows systems where global Python executables override local virtual environments\hich\f31506 \emdash \loch\f31506 
the application strictly binds execution to `.\\.venv\\Scripts\\python.exe`. System observability is maintained via a persi\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
stent dual-mode logger (`pipeline.log`), capturing operational flows at the `INFO` level and internal mathematical thresholds at the `DEBUG` level.
\par 
\par ---
\par 
